# This project needs no environment variables to run.
#
# `npm install && npm run dev` is sufficient. Everything below is optional, and the site behaves
# exactly as it always has when none of it is set.

# The canonical origin, used to make og:image absolute for WhatsApp, Slack and Twitter.
#
# Set this in the Vercel project if the site has a custom domain. Without it the code falls back to
# VERCEL_URL, which is the DEPLOYMENT hostname (…-a1b2c3.vercel.app) and changes on every push — so
# every share card would point at a URL that is not the one the reader has.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_ORIGIN=https://kitui2027.example.ke

# A passcode gate for the confidential document. See middleware.ts.
#
# UNSET MEANS OFF, and the site is open to anyone with the link — which is how it has always been.
# Set it and readers open the site once with ?k=<passcode>; a cookie carries them for thirty days.
# This raises the cost of an accidental forward; it is not authentication. For real access control
# use Vercel's own Password Protection, which sits in front of the deployment.
# SITE_PASSCODE=

# Optional, and only useful when hot reload misbehaves in a container:
#   DISABLE_HMR=true npm run dev
